<Base title="Sources and review">
  <div class="study">
    <p class="eyebrow">Research integrity</p><h1>Sources &amp; review</h1>
    <p class="lead">Published research will identify each primary passage, historical claim, interpretation, and contemporary inference.</p>
    <h2>Current state</h2>
    <p>No pilot comparison has yet been certified as source-checked. The initial outlines contain original paraphrases and research questions rather than extended Bible quotations or verified scholarly citations.</p>
    <h2>Planned bibliography</h2>
    <p>Each research claim will reference a specific biblical edition and, where warranted, academic literature with an author, title, publication year, and page or stable section. Manuscript questions and authorship disputes will receive separate notes.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>Conclusions will be versioned in Git, with interpretive changes documented rather than silently overwritten.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
